.TH MINSEC-SYNC 1 "" "minsec" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
minsec-sync \- report local minsec bans and maintain the crowd blocklist
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B minsec-sync
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B minsec-sync
is the opt-in multiplayer client for
.BR minsec (1).
It is a short-lived program intended to run periodically from a systemd timer.
It enrolls the host, reports new automatic bans from the daemon event log, and
loads a selected crowd blocklist into the dedicated nftables
.B crowd4
and
.B crowd6
sets.
.PP
The resident daemon contains no HTTP or TLS client.
Network activity and private signing-key management are isolated in this
helper.
Creating
.I /etc/minsec/sync.toml
is the opt-in switch used by the packaged timer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c " " \fIfile\fR ", " \-\-config " " \fIfile\fR
Read configuration from
.I file
instead of
.IR /etc/minsec/sync.toml .
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Print nftables scripts instead of passing them to
.BR nft (8).
This option only suppresses nftables changes.
It does not suppress HTTP requests, enrollment, reporting, key creation, or
state-file updates; a successful pull also advances its saved feed cursor.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the program version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS enroll
Create an Ed25519 signing key if necessary, solve the server's enrollment
proof-of-work challenge, and save the assigned host ID.
If this state is already present, print the existing host ID and return.
.PP
If the local host ID was lost but the server already knows the signing key,
the key is moved to
.I key.old
and enrollment is retried once with a new key.
.SS report
Read new automatic ban events from the configured minsec event log and submit
signed report batches.
The saved file cursor advances only after all batches succeed.
Manual bans are never reported.
Old or malformed events and networks broader than the reporting limits are
skipped.
.PP
Reports contain the attacker network, event time, filter/category, hit count,
and ban lifetime.
They do not contain log lines, usernames, or local user information.
IPv6 host addresses and prefixes narrower than /64 are aggregated to /64.
.SS pull
Fetch enabled IPv4 and IPv6 feeds for the configured tier, using saved ETags
and snapshot cursors when possible.
Full feeds atomically replace the corresponding set; delta feeds add and remove
individual entries.
If a delta cannot be applied, a full feed is fetched and installed.
.PP
This command manages only
.B crowd4
and
.B crowd6
in
.BR "table inet minsec" .
The daemon owns the chains and rules that reference those sets.
.SS run
Perform the timer workflow.
Enroll first if necessary, then report and/or pull according to configuration.
If the configuration file does not exist, exit successfully without output or
side effects.
This absent-file behavior is specific to
.BR run ;
the other commands report an error.
.SS status
Print the configured server, public key, enrollment host ID, next report
sequence number, event-log cursor, and saved feed state.
A private key is generated if one does not already exist.
.SH OPERATION
The packaged
.B minsec-sync.timer
runs
.B minsec-sync run
approximately every five minutes.
The service normally runs as the same
.B minsec
user as the daemon so it can read the event log and persistent state.
Pulling requires permission to execute
.BR nft (8)
and administer nftables, normally
.BR CAP_NET_ADMIN .
Enrollment, reporting, and pulling require HTTPS access to the configured
server and a usable CA trust store.
.PP
Disabling reporting or pulling does not remove existing crowd set entries.
To opt out completely, remove the sync configuration, stop or disable the
timer, and flush both crowd sets if immediate removal is desired:
.PP
.nf
nft flush set inet minsec crowd4
nft flush set inet minsec crowd6
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/minsec/sync.toml
Multiplayer configuration and opt-in marker.
.TP
.I /var/lib/minsec/events.jsonl
Default source of automatic ban events.
.TP
.I /var/lib/minsec/sync/key
Ed25519 private signing seed, created with mode 0600.
.TP
.I /var/lib/minsec/sync/key.old
Previous key retained after automatic recovery from lost enrollment state.
.TP
.I /var/lib/minsec/sync/state.json
Enrollment ID, report sequence and event cursor, and feed cursors.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/minsec/sync.toml.example
Packaged example configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/minsec-sync.service
Packaged one-shot service.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/minsec-sync.timer
Packaged periodic timer.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 when the requested operation succeeds.
.B run
also returns 0 when its configuration file is absent.
Configuration, state, network, server, feed, and nftables failures return 1.
.SH EXAMPLES
Opt in using the package example and test feed application visibly:
.PP
.nf
install -m 0644 /usr/share/doc/minsec/sync.toml.example /etc/minsec/sync.toml
minsec-sync enroll
minsec-sync --dry-run pull
systemctl enable --now minsec-sync.timer
.fi
.PP
Inspect client state:
.PP
.nf
minsec-sync status
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR minsec (1),
.BR minsec-sync.toml (5),
.BR minsec.toml (5),
.BR nft (8),
.BR systemd.timer (5)
